.env
# Everything the API produced stays out of git: the data-publishing rule is
# unresolved (one entrant reports organisers disallow Qloo responses in a
# public repo, another commits them). The pre-registration is the exception --
# it exists to be committed, and must be committed BEFORE the first real run.
out/*
# The registration AND every amendment are tracked. An amendment that lives
# only on disk proves nothing -- the point of the record is that a third party
# can see when a threshold moved and whether data had been seen by then.
!out/prereg.json
!out/prereg_amended_*.json
# Outcome data is public Wikimedia aggregate, not Qloo response data, and it
# is committed deliberately: collected before any Qloo call, it is only
# evidence of that if its timestamp is in the history.
!out/backtest_outcomes.json
!out/backtest_target.json
# Recorded preset runs are regenerated, and once they hold real Qloo responses
# the unresolved data-publishing rule applies to them too.
app/cache/*.json
